    "id": "l1_m4_h3_nu3_quadratic_frobenius_kernel",
    "title": "L1 m=4, h=3, nu=3 quadratic Frobenius kernel",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "In the clean nu=3 case, let J be the canonical antiderivative of cX^4U^2 with all p-multiple coefficients zero. There is a unique quadratic Q=q_2X^2+q_1X with q_2!=0 and q_2^p=a such that X^5U^3D=(X^4-Q)^p+J and X^5B_0=Q^p-J. Also ord_0(J)=5 and c=5U(0)D(0). Thus the wild Frobenius kernel has two scalar parameters. This node alone is a normal form; the proved tangent-radical successor excludes nu=3, while L1 remains open through other strata.",
